// mock:provider — `llm:inference`, scripted. Deterministic, free, offline.
//
// Correctness in this system cannot be paid for in tokens. A swarm test asks
// things like "twelve branches explore, branch seven wins, a pull request opens
// against the right base" — and with a real provider that test costs money every
// run, takes minutes, and ANSWERS DIFFERENTLY EACH TIME, which means it cannot
// assert the thing it exists to assert. Selection logic is untestable against a
// non-deterministic oracle.
//
// So this is the swap point being used for what it was designed for. The
// `llm:inference` world comment already anticipated it: "a deterministic mock
// provider imports nothing".
//
// It imports NO network, on purpose and provably: the world below has no
// `wasi:http`, so a test using it cannot accidentally reach a real provider and
// cannot spend anything. That is a stronger guarantee than remembering to set a
// fake base URL.
//
// Config (wasi:config/store):
//   mock-script  JSON. See src/lib.rs for the shape.
//   mock-model   what `describe` and the completions report, default "mock-1"
//
// What this is NOT: a substitute for running against a real provider. A scripted
// reply is exactly as realistic as whoever wrote it, and never produces the
// markdown fence around JSON, the truncated tool call, or the apology that a real
// model eventually will. Use it for LOGIC, and record a real run for REALISM —
// `artifact:cache` already keys derived work by its inputs, so a recorded
// response replays for free and exactly.
package mock:provider@0.1.0;

world mock-provider {
    export llm:inference/inference@0.1.0;
    import wasi:config/store@0.2.0-rc.1;
    /// So a rule can WAIT. A mock that answers in microseconds gives a load test
    /// the wrong shape entirely: real inference takes hundreds of milliseconds to
    /// seconds, and that latency is what decides how many branches are in flight
    /// at once, how long an environment is held, and whether anything queues.
    /// Stress-testing against an instant provider measures the harness.
    import wasi:clocks/monotonic-clock@0.2.0;
}
